    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A Transformer is usually fed by a high-voltage source and then steps down the voltage to a lower-voltage feed for low-voltage application (such as lights). Transformers also can step up voltage, but this generally does not apply to in building distribution."
      }
